9.2 Chapter 2 - A Technical Overview of lattice

9.2.1 Fig 2.1 Two conditioning variables
Oat yield by nitrogen, a panel per variety (columns) and block (rows): points joined by lines.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.1. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet-col :variety :facet-row :block}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter)]
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 700 :height 800})






9.2.2 Fig 2.2 One block
Source: Lattice Fig 2.2. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data (filterv #(= "I" (:block %)) oats)
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet :variety}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter)]
  :facets {:columns 3}
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 800 :height 450})






9.2.3 Fig 2.3 Banked to 45 degrees
Lattice’s aspect = "xy" chooses the panel shape from the slopes of the lines; here the image is narrow instead.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.3. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet-col :variety :facet-row :block}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter {:size 3})]
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 380 :height 800})






9.2.4 Fig 2.4 Eighteen panels in three rows
Source: Lattice Fig 2.4. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet #(str (:block %) " " (:variety %))}
  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter {:size 3})]
  :facets {:columns 6}
  :labels {:x "nitro" :y "yield"}}
 {:width 1000 :height 550})






9.2.5 Fig 2.5 Gaps between blocks
Lattice widens chosen gaps between panels (between); here each block is its own plot, arranged.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.5. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 (plot/arrange (for [block ["I" "II" "III" "IV" "V" "VI"]]
                 {:data (filterv #(= block (:block %)) oats)
                  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :facet :variety}
                  :charts [(chart/line) (chart/scatter {:size 3})]
                  :scales {:y {:domain [50 180]}}
                  :facets {:columns 3}
                  :labels {:title (str "Block " block) :x nil :y nil}})
               {:columns 2})
 {:width 1000 :height 700})






9.2.6 Fig 2.6 Dot plot
Barley yield of each variety at six sites, the two years in two shapes. Sites, varieties and years keep R’s factor order (nu/levels); lattice fills panels from the bottom, so the sites run top-down reversed.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.6. Data: Barley yields, Minnesota 1931-1932, R lattice package barley (Immer et al. 1934; Fisher 1971; Cleveland 1993); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (lattice).

(plot/render-image
 {:data barley
  :mapping {:x :yield :y :variety :shape :year :facet :site}
  :scales {:y {:domain (nu/levels :barley :variety)}
           :facet {:domain (vec (rseq (nu/levels :barley :site)))}
           :shape {:domain (nu/levels :barley :year)}}
  :charts [(chart/scatter)]
  :facets {:columns 1}
  :theme {:text {:tick-label {:size 8}}}
  :labels {:x "yield" :y nil}}
 {:width 600 :height 800})






9.2.7 Fig 2.7 Groups within panels
Source: Lattice Fig 2.7. Data: Oats yields: split-plot field trial, R MEMSS package Oats (Yates 1935; Pinheiro & Bates 2000); licence: GPL (&gt;= 2) (MEMSS).

(plot/render-image
 {:data oats
  :mapping {:x :nitro :y :yield :shape :variety :group :variety :facet :block}
  :charts [(chart/line {:color :darkgrey}) (chart/scatter {:color :black :size 6})]
  :facets {:columns 6}
  :labels {:title "Yield of three varieties of oats - a 3 x 4 split plot experiment with 6 blocks"
           :x "Nitrogen concentration (cwt/acre)" :y "Yield (bushels/acre)"}}
 {:width 1000 :height 400})






9.2.8 Fig 2.8 Stacked bars
Titanic passengers by class, stacked by survival, a panel per age and sex.
Source: Lattice Fig 2.8. Data: Titanic passengers and crew by class, sex, age and survival, R datasets package Titanic (Dawson 1995); licence: Part of R (GPL-2 | GPL-3).

(def titanic-panels ["Child Male" "Child Female" "Adult Male" "Adult Female"])


(plot/render-image
 {:data titanic
  :mapping {:x :n :y :class :color :survived :facet #(str (:age %) " " (:sex %))}
  :scales {:facet {:domain titanic-panels}}
  :charts [(chart/bar {:position :stack})]
  :facets {:columns 4}
  :theme {:panel {:grid {:x :none :y :none}}}
  :labels {:x "Freq" :y nil}}
 {:width 900 :height 350})






